<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Housing</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Housing</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Housing, Accommodation &amp; Neighborhood Platform (Phase B11). The platform's single owner
      of where a member is going to live and what it is like to live there.

      This is a relocation module, not a classifieds module, and the distinction is load-bearing.
      A listing is not an advert: it belongs to a landlord who may be a person, an agency, a hostel
      or an employer; it sits in a neighbourhood rather than at an address, because the address is
      the last thing revealed and the neighbourhood is the first thing asked about; it moves through
      a lifecycle from draft to occupied; and it is reached through a viewing before it is ever
      reserved, because nobody takes a home sight-unseen from a stranger on the internet.

      What Housing owns: housing listings, landlord profiles, viewings, reservations, neighbourhood
      profiles, neighbourhood insights, housing reports, the housing analytics rollup, and the
      accommodation-type and amenity catalogues. What it deliberately does not: the neighbourhood
      itself belongs to Location, the badge on a landlord belongs to Trust, the photograph bytes
      belong to Media, the agency behind a landlord belongs to Providers, the discussion about a
      neighbourhood belongs to Community, the explainer beside a listing belongs to Guides, and the
      jobs and goods near a home belong to Jobs and Marketplace. Housing reaches every one of them
      through published contracts and stores identifiers, never copies.

      The neighbourhood is the module's central claim, and its ownership is split deliberately.
      Location (B4) owns the *place* — the administrative node, its slug, its hierarchy path and its
      centroid. Housing owns the *profile* — the living summaries, the liveability indexes and the
      moderated community insights — keyed by B4's AreaId and never duplicating a single geographic
      fact. The profile is published through INeighborhoodDirectory so Jobs, Marketplace, Providers,
      Guides, Community and future modules can consume a neighbourhood without referencing this
      module's aggregates and without any of them owning the concept.

      Search is a seam, not an engine: the module ships an EF-backed search over the write model and
      the IHousingSearchEngine port an OpenSearch adapter can satisfy later without a domain change.
      Accommodation types, amenities, ranking, fraud signals, insight moderation, address disclosure,
      availability calendars and neighbourhood metric sources are contributor seams on the same
      terms.

      Payment processing, lease management, digital signatures, mortgages, property valuation, map
      provider integration, AI recommendations and commute calculation are explicitly out of scope,
      and the abstractions here are shaped so each arrives as a new module or a new adapter rather
      than as a restructuring of this one.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, the
      Identity module, Trust, Location, Media, Community, Providers, Guides, Jobs, Marketplace, or
      Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    B10's reference set, minus Marketplace. Location, Media, Community, Providers and Guides are
    deliberate and documented. B11 consumes Location's published Integration and Extensibility
    contracts (IGeographicScopeResolver, INearbyResourceProvider, ILocationResourceCounter, and the
    administrative-area catalogue that owns the neighbourhood itself), Media's published reference
    contracts (attach-by-reference, never URLs — and MediaOwnerType.HousingListing has existed since
    B5), Community's published Extensibility contract (ICommunityContentSource — and
    CommunityContentType.Housing has existed since B6), Providers' published IProviderDirectory for
    the agencies and hostels behind a landlord, and Guides' published IGuideDirectory for the
    renting-safely explainers beside a listing.

    Notably absent: the Identity module, the Trust module, the Jobs module and the Marketplace
    module. Housing reaches Identity through the kernel's ICurrentUser and Trust through
    Diaspora.Contracts — the published ITrustVerificationSubmission contract and Trust's published
    integration events — never through their aggregates. Jobs and Marketplace are not consumed at
    all: they are sibling verticals, and a reference to either would be the first edge in the graph
    B2.6 exists to keep acyclic. "Nearby jobs" and "neighbourhood marketplace" are answered through
    Location's INearbyResourceProvider registry, which both siblings already contribute to and
    neither knows Housing reads. Architecture tests enforce all five.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Location\Diaspora.Modules.Location.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Media\Diaspora.Modules.Media.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Community\Diaspora.Modules.Community.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Providers\Diaspora.Modules.Providers.csproj" />
